1031:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_i2c.c ****     This subsection provides a set of functions allowing to manage the I2C data
1032:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_i2c.c ****     transfers.
1033:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_i2c.c **** 
1034:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_i2c.c ****     (#) There are two modes of transfer:
1035:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (++) Blocking mode : The communication is performed in the polling mode.
1036:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_i2c.c ****             The status of all data processing is returned by the same function
1037:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_i2c.c ****             after finishing transfer.
1038:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (++) No-Blocking mode : The communication is performed using Interrupts
1039:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_i2c.c ****             or DMA. These functions return the status of the transfer startup.
1040:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_i2c.c ****             The end of the data processing will be indicated through the
1041:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_i2c.c ****             dedicated I2C IRQ when using Interrupt mode or the DMA IRQ when
1042:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_i2c.c ****             using DMA mode.
1043:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_i2c.c **** 
1044:Drivers/STM32F7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f7xx_hal_i2c.c ****     (#) Blocking mode functions are :
